behind.content:
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|ahind||dialect}}
* {{alt|en|behine||archaic|AAVE}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|behinde}}, {{m|enm|behinden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|behindan|t=on the back side of, behind}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*bihindan}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*bihindini|t=on the back side of, in the rear of, behind}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*bi-}} + {{m|gmw-pro|*hindō|t=the hind side, back part}}, equivalent to {{pre|en|be|hind}}. Compare {{cog|osx|bihindan|t=behind|pos=adverb}}, {{noncog|gmh|behinter|t=behind; back}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|preposition|adverb|noun}}
** {{IPA|en|/bɪˈhaɪnd/|/bəˈhaɪnd/|a=RP}}
** {{IPA|en|/beˈhəɪn/|/beˈhoɪn/|/beˈhaɪn/|a=Local Dublin}}
** {{audio|en|En-uk-behind.ogg|a=UK}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈbiˌhaɪnd/|/biˈhaɪnd/|/bɪˈhaɪnd/|/bəˈhaɪnd/|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-behind.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|be|hind}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪnd|s=2}}

===Preposition===
{{en-head|prep}}

# At or to the [[back]] or far side of.
#: {{ant|en|in front of}}
#: {{ux|en|The children were hiding '''behind''' the wall.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Behind''' the garage needs clearing asap.}}
#: {{ux|en|The sun went '''behind''' the clouds.}}
#: {{ux|en|Look '''behind''' you!}}
#: {{ux|en|I hide '''behind''' you in hide and seek.}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=But then I had the [massive] flintlock by me for protection. <br>{{...}}The linen-press and a chest on the top of it formed, however, a very good gun-carriage; and, thus mounted, aim could be taken out of the window{{nb...}}, and a 'bead' could be drawn upon Molly, the dairymaid, kissing the fogger '''behind''' the hedge, little dreaming that the deadly tube was levelled at them.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-19|author=w:Timothy Garton Ash|volume=189|issue=6|page=18|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=Where Dr Pangloss meets Machiavelli
|url=http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/jul/10/geopolitics-transatlantic-trade-deal
|passage=Hidden '''behind''' thickets of acronyms and gorse bushes of detail, a new great game is under way across the globe. Some call it geoeconomics, but it's geopolitics too. The current power play consists of an extraordinary range of countries simultaneously sitting down to negotiate big free trade and investment agreements.}}
#: {{synonyms|en|in back of|q1=US|to the [[rear]] of|a-back|q3=Chester}}
#: {{antonyms|en|in front of}}
## {{lb|en|figuratively}} Concealed by (something serving as a facade or disguise).
##: {{ux|en|'''Behind''' the smile was a cruel intention.}}
## {{lb|en|figuratively}} In the past, from the viewpoint of.
##: {{ux|en|All my problems are '''behind''' me.}}
# Less forward or advanced than; [[after]].
#: {{antonyms|en|ahead of}}
## After in physical progress or [[distance]].
##: ''Smith finished the race a lap '''behind''' the others.''
##* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island| passage=About the center, and a good way '''behind''' the rest, Silver and I followed — I tethered by my rope{{nb...}}.}}
## After in developmental progress, score, grade, etc.; inferior to.
##: {{ux|en|I'm ranked sixth in the French class, '''behind''' five other pupils.}}
##: {{ux|en|In the cricket match, England are 120 runs '''behind''' India.}}
##* {{RQ:King James Version|book=2 Corinthians|chapter=11|verse=5|passage=For I suppose I was not a whit '''behind''' the very chiefest apostles.}}
## After in [[time]].
##: ''London is nine hours '''behind''' Tokyo.''
# [[responsible|Responsible]] for, being the creator or controller of.
#: {{ux|en|Who is '''behind''' these terrorist attacks?}}
#: {{ux|en|Mr Jones was the man '''behind''' the redevelopment plan.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2023| author=Ian Miller|magazine=OutKick| url=https://www.outkick.com/bud-light-replaces-marketing-vp-behind-dylan-mulvaney-partnership/| passage=Bud Light replaces Marketing VP '''behind''' Dylan Mulvaney partnership.}}
# Underlying, being the reason for or explanation of.
#: {{ux|en|What is '''behind''' this unexpected decision?}}
# In [[support]] of.
#: {{ux|en|The republicans are fully '''behind''' their candidate.}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes regarded as|_|non-standard|US|informal}} [[following|Following]], subsequent to; [[as a result of|as a result]] or [[consequence]] of; [[because of]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=DeShawn Dorsey|title=Longsuffering Through Emotional Wounds|page=40|passage=He was like, 'Fuck the police! Fuck you! You know who I am, you gonna quit playing with me, bitch.' I'm like let's go. 'Cause I wasn't trying to go to jail '''behind''' that shit.}}

