canteen.content:
==English==
[[File:Defense.gov photo essay 100818-A-7341H-041.jpg|thumb|Drinking from a canteen or water flask of late 20th century or early 21st century design. Note the attached [[stopper]].]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|cantine}}, itself borrowed from {{der|en|it|cantina}}. {{doublet|en|cantina}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kænˈtiːn/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-canteen.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/kænˈtin/|a=GA}}
** {{IPA|en|[kʰɛə̯nˈtʰin]|a=US,æ-tensing}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːn|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|bottle}} A [[water bottle]], [[flask]], or other [[vessel]], typically used by a [[soldier]] or [[camper]] as a [[bottle]] for carrying [[water]] or [[liquor]] for [[drink]].
#* {{Q|en|John Williamson Palmer|{{w|Stonewall Jackson's Way|Stonewall Jackson's Way}}|quote=Come, stack arms, Men! Pile on the rails; stir up the campfire bright; no matter if the '''canteen''' fails, we'll make a roaring night. Here Shenandoah brawls along, there burly Blue Ridge echoes strong, to swell the Brigade's rousing song, of “Stonewall Jackson’s Way.”|year=1862}}
# A [[military]] [[mess kit]].
# A [[box]] with [[compartment]]s for [[storing]] eating [[utensil]]s, [[silverware]] etc.
# A [[temporary]] or [[mobile]] [[café]] used in an [[emergency]] or on a film [[location]] etc.
# A small [[cafeteria]] or [[snack bar]], especially one in a [[military]] establishment, school, or place of work.
#: {{ux|en| He ordered a salad at the '''canteen'''.}}
## A [[cafeteria]] in a school or place of work.
## Goods purchased from a [[prison]] canteen.
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=29 Dec 84|volume=12|number=25|journal=Gay Community News|page=6|title=Prisons and Roles|author=Mykki Balduff|text=Yeah, I worked that bitch. She was buying me all the '''canteen''' I wanted.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=23 Nov 15|work=Pen America|title=Dark Corners|author=Melvin L. Boone|url=https://pen.org/dark-corners/|text=“Well, le’me give you some advice,” he continued. “If someone offers you some '''canteen''', don’t take it.”<br>I instinctively knew what he was warning me against. But I felt slightly disrespected because it wasn’t as if I were a frail young girl who might go out on a date with someone and feel obligated to have sex because the guy had bought me a Happy Meal. The way I saw it, if someone wanted to give me some '''canteen''', I was getting something for nothing!|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260120190721/https://pen.org/dark-corners/|archivedate=20 January 2026}}
##* {{RQ:Reddit|en|date=11 Sep 24|handle=Jordangander|subreddit=Prison|id=1fdvaoz|commentid=lmnxz5x|title=More about solitary: I get conflicting results when I look up what modern solitary is like...?|passage=Administrative Confinement, sort of like a jail inside the prison, this is for those waiting on disciplinary court for a violation, or under investigation, plus other things. 2 man cells, allowed your tablets, some property, some '''canteen''' including food, reading books. 4 hours outside exercise weekly after 30 days.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241007201805/https://www.reddit.com/r/Prison/comments/1fdvaoz/comment/lmnxz5x/|archivedate=7 October 2024}}

