# An act of shopping, especially routine shopping for food and other domestic supplies.
#: {{ux|en|This is where I do my weekly '''shop'''.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|colloquial}} The collective items bought (or to be bought) on a shopping [[trip]].
#: {{ux|en|I’ve got a big '''shop''', so feel free to go in front.}}

====Usage notes====
In [[North America]] establishments that sell goods are mainly referred to as [[store]]s with "shop" only used for smaller establishments.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|establishment that sells goods}} {{l|en|boutique}}, {{l|en|retail}} [[outlet]], [[store]] {{lb|en|US|and|Canada}}; see also [[Thesaurus:retail store]]
* {{sense|place where things are crafted}} {{l|en|atelier}}, {{l|en|studio}}, {{l|en|workshop}}
* {{sense|automobile mechanic's workplace}} {{l|en|garage}}
* {{sense|workplace}} {{l|en|office}}, place of work, [[workplace]]
* {{sense|wood shop}} {{l|en|carpentry}}, {{l|en|wood shop}}, {{l|en|woodwork}}
* {{sense|metal shop}} {{l|en|metal shop}}, {{l|en|metalwork}}, {{l|en|machine shop}}

