beside.content:
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|beside}}, {{m|enm|besiden}}, {{m|enm|bisyde}} (also {{m|enm|besides}} > {{l|en|besides}}), from {{inh|en|ang|[[be]] [[sīdan]]}}, {{m|ang|[[bī]] [[sīdan]]|t=by the side (of), on the side (of)}}. Compare {{cog|stq|biesiede|t=aside}}, {{cog|nds-de|bisied|t=aside}}, {{cog|de|beiseite|t=aside, to one side}}. Compare also {{cog|nl|terzijde|t=aside}}. {{surf|+pre|en|be|side}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈsaɪd/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈsaɪd/|/biˈsaɪd/|/bəˈsaɪd/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-beside.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈsʌɪd/|a=CA,idle-idol split}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪd|s=2}}

===Preposition===
{{en-head|prep}}

# [[next to|Next to]]; at the [[side]] of.
#: {{ux|en|A small table '''beside''' the bed}}
# Not [[relevant]] to.
#: {{ux|en|That is [[beside the point|'''beside''' the point]] / '''beside''' the topic / '''beside''' the subject / '''beside''' the focus of this discussion.}}
#* {{see citations|en}}
# [[besides|Besides]]; [[in addition to]].
#: {{ant|en|aside}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll need another dictionary '''beside''' this one.}}

====Usage notes====
* Not to be confused with {{m|en|besides}}. See {{w|Adverbial genitive}}.

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|besideness|therebeside|besidely|beside oneself|besides|beside the mark|beside the point}}

====Translations====
{{trans-see|next to}}

{{trans-top|not relevant to}}
