===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=final|:inh|enm:laste<id:finally>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|laste}}, {{m|enm|latst}}, syncopated variant of {{m|enm|latest}}, both ultimately from {{inh|en|ang|latost}}. {{dbt|en|latest}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[final|Final]], [[ultimate]], coming after all others of its kind.
#: {{ux|en|Will try to fix it [[by oneself|by myself]] for now: as a [[last resort|'''last''' resort]], we can always take it to a [[grease monkey]].}}
#: {{ux|en|''Eyes Wide Shut'' was the '''last''' film to be directed by Stanley Kubrick.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=V|passage=Then everybody once more knelt, and soon the blessing was pronounced. The choir and the clergy trooped out slowly, {{...}}, down the nave to the western door. {{...}} At a seemingly immense distance the surpliced group stopped to say the '''last''' prayer.}}
# Most [[recent]], [[latest]], last so far.
#: {{ux|en|The '''last''' time I saw him, he was married.}}
#: {{ux|en|I have received your note dated the 17th '''last''', and am responding to say that{{...}}|q=archaic usage}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Vanity Fair|passage=She told him the '''last''' news about little Georgy, and how he was gone to spend that very day with his sisters in the country.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=25 May 2013|title=No Hiding Place|url=http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21578357-plan-assess-peoples-personal-characteristics-their-twitter-streams-no|volume=407|issue=8837|page=74|passage=In America alone, people spent $170 billion on “direct marketing”—junk mail of both the physical and electronic varieties—'''last''' year.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20171025020559/https://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21578357-plan-assess-peoples-personal-characteristics-their-twitter-streams-no|archivedate=25 October 2017}}
# Farthest of all from a given [[quality]], [[character]], or [[condition]]; most [[unlikely]], or least [[preferable]].
#: {{ux|en|He is the '''last''' person to be accused of theft.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''last''' person I want to meet is Helen.}}
#: {{ux|en|More rain is the '''last''' thing we need right now.}}
# Being the only one remaining of its class.
#: {{ux|en|Japan is the '''last''' empire.}}
# Supreme; highest in degree; utmost.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1802|author=[[w:Robert Hall (minister)|Robert Hall]]|title=Reflections on War|passage=Contending for principles of the '''last''' importance.}}
# Lowest in rank or degree.
#: {{ux|en|Three contestants will win awards, but the '''last''' prize is just a book voucher.}}
#* {{RQ:Cumberland Posthumous Works|volume=II|scene=[iii]|page=237|passage=In one word then, unless I could unfold the mystery, I will not wish you to consider me but as the '''last''' and lowest of mankind.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1899|author=[[w:Richard Henry Savage|Richard Savage]]|title=The White Lady of Khaminavatka: A Story of the Ukraine|page=186|passage=The whole community from the patrician master to the '''last''' beggar knew that in the five months when the generous bosom of the steppe throbbed with creative life, they must toil for the subsistence of all {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=w:Julius Fast|title=Body Language|isbn=9780671673253|page=39|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=yqx1j8ynGfwC&pg=PA39|passage=Lesser, but still important executives had offices without corner windows. The rank below this had offices without windows at all. {{...}} The '''last''' rank had desks out in an open room.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=31 March 2003|author=Marko Peljhan|chapter=Lecture: March 31, 2003|editors=Jen Budney; Adrian Blackwell|title=Unboxed Engagements in Social Space|year_published=2005|isbn=1896183131|page=110|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=EFkAYgXs2JoC&pg=PA110|passage=Russia is a very different place than here. {{...}} Even the '''last''' soldier knows who Malevich was, and what the ''Black Square'' is, since they were taught this in school.}}

