===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|da|gmq-oda|at}}, from {{inh|da|non|at}}. Cognate with {{cog|sv|att}}, {{cog|no|at}}. Probably from {{inh|da|gem-pro|*þat}}, a demonstrative pronoun used as a conjunction; compare {{cog|jut|te,de}}, {{cog|en|that}}, {{cog|de|dass}}, {{cog|nl|dat}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|da|/at/|[æd̥]|[æ]}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|da|conjunction}}

# [[that]] {{q|introduces a {{glossary|noun clause}} functioning as the subject, object or predicative of a verb, or as the object of a prepositional phrase}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1986|author=Knud Erik Larsen|title=Bare ikke om søndagen|url=https://books.google.dk/books?id=DedIDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT85
|passage=Knud hørte, '''at''' bedstefaren lagde værktøjet fra sig
|translation=Knud heard '''that''' his grandfather put down the tool.}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1876|author=J.P. Jacobsen|title=Fru Marie Grubbe|volume=1|page=67|url=https://books.google.dk/books?id=VdK9DgAAQBAJ&pg=PT59
|passage=Hun var overbevist om '''at''' det var sandt.
|translation=She was convinced '''that''' it was true.}}
# {{lb|da|archaic}} [[that]], [[in order that]], [[so that]] {{q|introduces an {{glossary|adverbial clause}} stating the purpose}}
#* '''1856''', Christian Winther, ''Hr. Peder Jernskjæg'', from ''Hjortens Flugt'' / https://kalliope.org/da/text/winther2018100610:
#*: Og Hjorten vil jeg fange, | At Korset jeg kan faae.
#*:: And the deer, I will catch, that I may win the cross.
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1987|author=Thomas Bruun|title=Et paradisisk blik. Humoresker og grotesker
|passage=det er helvedes svært, '''at''' du bare ved det.
|translation=it is damned difficult, just '''that''' you know it.}}
#: {{synonyms|da|for at}}
# [[that]], [[so that]] {{q|introduces an {{glossary|adverbial clause}} stating the result, normally after a demonstrative adverb or pronoun}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1902|author=Karin Michaëlis|title=Barnet|url=https://books.google.dk/books?id=A_4kDgAAQBAJ&pg=PT62
|passage=Jeg er saa fattig, '''at''' jeg sulter paa Sjæl og Legeme.
|translation=I am so poor '''that''' I starve in my soul and my body.}}
#: {{synonyms|da|så at|således at}}
# [[that]], [[why]] {{q|introducing an {{glossary|independent clause}}, expressing passion, surprise, anger, or joy}}
#* {{quote-book|da|year=1901|author=Herman Bang|title=Det graa Hus|url=https://books.google.dk/books?id=xpqmDgAAQBAJ&pg=PT26
|passage='''At''' De kan synge saa tidligt om Morgenen.
|translation='''That''' you can sing that early in the morning.}}
# {{lb|da|proscribed}} {{non-gloss|added pleonastically to other conjunctions: {{l|da|fordi|fordi at}}, {{l|da|hvis|hvis at}}, {{l|da|når|når at}}}}
#* '''2009''', Frank Colding, Sejleren, p. 32 / https://books.google.dk/books?id=HCNperkZeKIC&pg=PA32:
#*: Forbavset aner min forstand, | at denne scenes sære magt | kun begribes, '''hvis at''' man | bevæger sig i dansetakt.
#*:: Astonished, my mind senses that the strange power of this scene can only be understood '''if''' one moves in dance steps.

====References====
