{{inh+|da|gmq-oda|at}}, from {{inh|da|non|at}}, cognate with {{cog|sv|att}}, {{cog|no|å}}. Originally the same word as the preposition {{inh|da|non|at||at, to}}, from {{inh|da|gem-pro|*at}}, cognate with {{cog|en|at}}. {{doublet|da|ad}}). In the West Germanic languages, a different preposition, {{m|gem-pro|*tō||to}}, serves as the infinitive marker, cf {{cog|en|to}}, {{cog|de|zu}}, {{cog|nl|te}}.

