begin.content:
{{also|Begin|Bégin}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|beginnen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|beginnan||to begin}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*biginnan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*biginnaną||to begin}}, from {{l|en|be-}} + base verb {{m|gem-pro||*ginnaną}} also found in {{cog|ang|onginnan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈɡɪn/|/bəˈɡɪn/|/biˈɡɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-to begin.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-begin.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪn|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|+|~ning|began|begun}}

# {{lb|en|ergative}} To [[start]], to [[initiate]] or take the [[first]] step into something.
#: {{ux|en|I '''began''' playing the piano at the age of five.|q=''transitive''}}
#: {{ux|en|Now that everyone is here, we should '''begin''' the presentation.|q=''transitive''}}
#: {{ux|en|The program '''begins''' at 9 o’clock on the dot.|q=''intransitive''}}
#: {{ux|en|I rushed to get to class on time, but the lesson had already '''begun'''.|q=''intransitive''}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Malebranche|paragraph=41|page=175|passage=The Apoſtle '''begins''' our Knowledge in the Creatures, which lead us to the Knowledge of God, if we will make uſe of our Reaſon: [...]}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Works 1751|volume=I|title=Messiah|lines=1–2|page=37|passage=Ye Nymphs of Solyma! '''begin''' the ſong: / To heav'nly themes ſublimer ſtrains belong.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=IV|page=48|passage=Mr. Cooke at once '''began''' a tirade against the residents of Asquith for permitting a sandy and generally disgraceful condition of the roads. So roundly did he vituperate the inn management in particular, and with such a loud flow of words, that I trembled lest he should be heard on the veranda.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=5|passage=Of all the queer collections of humans outside of a crazy asylum, it seemed to me this sanitarium was the cup winner. {{...}} When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you '''begin''' to get queer, I suppose.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Nicky Gregson|title=Living with Things: Ridding, Accommodation, Dwelling|page=48
|passage=As Andrew, in particular, '''began''' to work on renovation and improvement, his talk about this '''began''' to be peppered with references to 'bodgery' &mdash; 'When I look at it, all I see is bodgery, he says recurrently, with a mixture of exclamation and despair.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=2008-04-09|author=Yudhijit Bhattacharjee|title=Harnessing Biology, and Avoiding Oil, for Chemical Goods|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2008/04/09/technology/techspecial/09chem.html
|passage=Similarly, the biotech giant Cargill has '''begun''' manufacturing a polymer from vegetable oils that is used in polyurethane foams, which is found in beddings, furniture and car-seat headrests.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506152457/https://www.nytimes.com/2008/04/09/technology/techspecial/09chem.html|archivedate=6 May 2025}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|title=Beating the Odds: The Rise, Fall, and Resurrection of a Sports Handicapper|author=Brandon Lang; Stanley Cohen|ISBN=1602396809|passage=State '''begins''' fouling and UCLA misses a couple of front-end free throws on one-and-ones. }}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-06-29|volume=407|issue=8842|page=29
|title=Unspontaneous combustion
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/asia/21580154-forest-fires-bring-record-levels-air-pollution-and-end-not-sight-unspontaneous
|passage=Since the mid-1980s, when Indonesia first '''began''' to clear its bountiful forests on an industrial scale in favour of lucrative palm-oil plantations, “haze” has become an almost annual occurrence in South-East Asia.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[come]] into [[existence]].
#* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Man|passage=Vast chain of being! which from God '''began'''.}}

====Conjugation====
{{en-conj|past=began|stem=beginn|past_ptc=begun|old=1|past_2sg_old2=begannest}}

====Synonyms====
* See [[Thesaurus:begin]].

