===Etymology===
From {{bor|cy|en|pyramid}}, from {{der|cy|fr|pyramide}}, from {{der|cy|fro|piramide}}, from {{der|cy|la|pyramis|pȳramis, pȳramidis}}, from {{der|cy|grc|πῡραμίς}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/ˈpɨ̞ramɪd/|a=cy-N}}
* {{IPA|cy|/ˈpɪramɪd/|a=cy-S}}

====Usage notes====
Being a word borrowed from English derived from Greek, the ''y'' in ''pyramid'' is pronounced /ɨ̞, ɪ/ rather than expected /ə/. To preserve consistency between pronunciation and spelling, some prefer to spell this word {{l|cy|puramid}}. Nevertheless, ''pyramid'' is the more common spelling of the two. See {{l|cy|symbol}}/{{l|cy|sumbol}}, {{l|cy|synthesis}}/{{l|cy|sunthesis}}, {{l|cy|system}}/{{l|cy|sustem}} for similar examples.

