* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-helper.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{wp|[[Bank engine|+ (loco)]]}}
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[help]]s; an [[aide]]; [[assistant]]; [[auxiliary]].
# That which helps; anything serving to [[assist]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2005|work=PC World|volume=23|page=158|passage=While Adobe's Acrobat Reader, Macromedia's Flash player, and other common plug-ins suggest themselves the moment you encounter a site that requires them, other browser '''helpers''' are harder to find.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Jude Deveraux|title=The Mulberry Tree|page=84|passage=He no longer liked food that had “helper” in the name, such as Hamburger '''Helper''' and Tuna '''Helper'''. Patsy said he'd become uppity, and maybe, when it came to food, he had.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Neale Blackwood|title=Advanced Excel Reporting for Management Accountants|page=154|passage=If a particular calculation is to be used a few times, it makes sense to put it in a '''helper''' cell so that it can be referred to by other formulas.}}
# {{lb|en|Singapore|Hong Kong|Philippines}} A person who does cleaning and cooking in a family home, or in a market; domestic employee.
# {{lb|en|rail|US}} A [[locomotive]] that assists a [[train]], usually on steep gradients.
#: {{syn|en|banker}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1964|month=November|title=Automatic '''helper''' locomotive control on the Louisville & Nashville RR, USA|journal=Modern Railways|page=354|text=A device for the automatic control of crewless '''helper''' locomotives cut into the make-up of heavy freight trains has been perfected by the Louisville & Nashville RR in conjunction with the General Railway Signalling Co.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A stimulating [[pill]], especially [[amphetamine]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Priscilla Presley; Sandra Harmon|title=w:Elvis and Me|year=1985|publisher=Putnam|page=152|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/elvismep00pres/page/152/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-399-12984-1|passage=And I routinely took more “'''helpers'''” when I woke up in order to maintain the fast pace and, more importantly, to study for my final exams.}}

