desk.content:
==English==
[[Image:Hermann Hesse Desk Museum Gaienhofen.jpeg|thumb|250px|A [[typewriter]] on a desk]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|deske}}, {{m|enm|desque}}, from {{der|en|la-med|desca}}, modified from {{der|en|roa-oit|desco}}, from {{der|en|la|discus}}. {{doublet|en|dais|disc|discus|dish|disk|diskos}}. See also {{der|en|de|Tisch}}, "table".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɛsk/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-desk.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛsk|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wp}}

# A [[table]], [[frame]], or [[case]], in past centuries usually with a sloping top but now usually with a flat top, for the use of [[writer]]s and [[reader]]s. It often has a [[drawer]] or [[repository]] underneath.
#: {{ux|en|She organized her notes neatly on her '''desk''' before starting the project.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''desk''' was cluttered with papers and books, making it hard to concentrate.}}
