===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[at no time|At no time]]; on no [[occasion]]; in no [[circumstance]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:never}}
#: {{ux|en|We can '''never''' repay your many kindnesses, [[thank you]].}}
#: {{ux|en|I finally finished, and I '''never''' do wanna do it again.}}
#: {{ux|en|We were at the same college, but happened '''never''' to meet.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll '''never''' not like you.}}
#* {{RQ:Fletcher Shakespeare Two Noble Kinsmen|2|4|text=Why should I love this Gentleman? Tis odds / He '''never''' will affect me;}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=1|passage=In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He '''never''' read me any of his manuscripts,&nbsp;[&hellip;], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1908|author=w:Lucy Maud Montgomery|title=Anne of Green Gables|section=[[s:Anne of Green Gables (1908)/Chapter XXI|Chapter XXI: A New Departure in Flavorings]]|passage="I '''never''' thought you were so fond of Mr. Phillips that you'd require two handkerchiefs to dry your tears just because he was going away," said Marilla.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author=B. G. Jefferis; J. L. Nichols|title=[[s:Searchlights on Health/Sensible Rules for the Nurse|Searchlights on Health: Sensible Rules for the Nurse]]
|passage='''Never''' speak of the symptoms of your patient in his presence, unless questioned by the doctor, whose orders you are always to obey ''implicitly''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|url=https://archive.org/details/timetohealautobi00ford/|year=1980|author=w:Gerald Ford|chapter=Boyhood—and Beyond|title=A Time to Heal|location=[[New York]]|publisher=w:Berkley Books|ISBN=0-425-04693-1|page=95|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/timetohealautobi00ford/page/95/
|text="You don't believe the Soviet Union is going to reduce its defense budget, do you?" Boggs asked.<br>Premier Chou didn't wait for the translator to finish. "'''Never''', '''never''', '''never'''," he replied in perfect English.}}
# Not at any [[other]] time; not on any other occasion; not [[previously]].
#* {{quote-book|en|date=November 30 1601|author=w:Elizabeth I of England|title=s:Elizabeth I's Farewell Speech
|passage=There is no jewel, be it of '''never''' so rich a price, which I set before this jewel: I mean your love.}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Pride and Prejudice|4|text="He is just what a young man ought to be," said she, "sensible, good-humoured, lively; and I '''never''' saw such happy manners!--so much ease, with such perfect good breeding!"}}
#* '''1908''', {{w|Lucy Maud Montgomery}}, ''[[s:Anne of Green Gables (1908)/Chapter XIII|Anne of Green Gables]]'', Chapter XIII: The Delights of Anticipation,
#*: I '''never''' saw such an infatuated man.
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Negative particle (''used to negate verbs in the simple past tense; also used [[absolutely]]'').
#: {{ux|en|The police say I stole the car, but I '''never''' did it.}}
#: {{ux|en|You said you were going to mow the lawn today. – I '''never'''!}}<!--example of "never" used absolutely in this sense-->
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1905|author=E. W. Horning|title=A Thief in the Night
|passage="You're '''never''' going to break in?"<br>"This instant, if you'll, help me; in five or ten minutes, if you won't."}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1976|artist=Rod Hart|title=C.B. Savage|text=Well I looked at Jay and I said "hey, did you hear what I just heard?"<br>He nodded his head and his face turned red and he '''never''' said a word}}

