=====Usage notes=====
* Unlike in Modern English, using ''for'' to express the duration of an event (as per sense 2 above) is relatively uncommon in Old English. Using a time noun phrase in the accusative case, with no preposition, is much more common: ''Wē wunodon '''fīf dagas''' on þām sċræfe'' ("We stayed in that cave '''for five days'''").

